# The counter above the shell (roadmap l4.md L2): a program that never waits
# starves every thread below it, and only those. No process runs, init's
# thread included, so the shell never starts (os-server.md P12), while the
# kernel and the OS server go on: the kernel's ticks end the test.
program: shell
define: TEST_COUNTER_ABOVE
define: TEST_THREAD_REPORT
define: TEST_END_TICKS=100
---
rx286, test build
rx286: thread root ran
rx286: thread printer ran
rx286: thread mouse ran
rx286: thread console ran
rx286: thread kbd ran
rx286: thread fd ran
rx286: thread hd ran
rx286: thread serial ran
rx286: thread sound ran
rx286: thread rtc ran
rx286: thread counter ran
rx286: thread os ran
rx286: thread os ran
rx286: thread disk ran
rx286: thread disk ran
rx286: thread disk ran
rx286: thread os ran
rx286: thread os ran
rx286: thread thread did not run
